g {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/UNK.png"}] "UNK"]]] [:tr {:class "hidden_referees", :style "display: none"} [:th {} "Judge / Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5004830"} "W. Than Yin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/UNK"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/UNK.png"}] "UNK"]]] [:tr {:class "hidden_referees", :style "display: none"} [:th {} "Judge / Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5004831"} "W. Van Eecken"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The change of weight limit for this class proved beneficial to the Czechoslovak boxer, " [:a {:href "/athletes/8281"} "Július Torma"] ", for it allowed him to make the welterweight division and not fight at " [:a {:href "/results/22384"} "middleweight"] ", where the opposition was expected to be stronger. Torma’s charge to the title was nearly ended in the 2nd round by the skull of his Canadian opponent. Angered by what he considered the unsportsmanlike behavior of " [:a {:href "/athletes/1144"} "Clifford Blackburn"] " before the fight, Torma bludgeoned his opponent throughout but, the coup-de-grace, a left hook, fractured a bone in his hand. The defensive skills of Torma proved sufficient to bring him to the final and a meeting with " [:a {:href "/athletes/8691"} "Hank Herring"] " of the USA."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In a disappointing Olympic Games for the American team, Herring was the only boxer to reach a final, but he couldn’t turn silver into gold and Czechoslovakia celebrated their first Olympic boxing title. Torma was born in Hungary and moved to Czechoslovakia after the war. He went on to win the 1949 European title, and retired after a career of 997 fights with just 60 losses. He won 13 Hungarian and 10 Czech titles. He returned to the Olympic arena twice more, but was eliminated at the quarter-final stage on both occasions."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/4108"} "Alessandro D’Ottavio"] " of Italy, the bronze medal winner, was most successful as a professional, winning his national light-heavyweight title, whilst " [:a {:href "/athletes/4829"} "Gunnar Hansen"] ", a first round loser, became a legendary figure in Norwegian boxing and was awarded the Olympic Order in bronze for his achievements in and out of the ring."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/8281"} "Július Torma"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TCH"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TCH.png"}] "TCH"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/8691"} "Hank Herring"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/4108"} "Alessandro D'Ottavio"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/7966"} "Duggie Du Preez"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RSA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu